[[:db/retract 17592186149955 :answer-field/choices 17592186149956] [:db/retract 17592186149955 :answer-field/choices 17592186149957] [:db/retract 17592186149955 :answer-field/choices 17592186149958] [:db/retract 17592186149955 :answer-field/choices 17592186149959] [:db/retract 17592186149950 :answer-field/choices 17592186149952] [:db/retract 17592186149950 :answer-field/choices 17592186149953] [:db/retract 17592186149950 :answer-field/choices 17592186149954] [:db/retract 17592186149950 :answer-field/choices 17592186149951] [:db/retract 17592186149939 :answer-field/choices 17592186149940] [:db/retract 17592186149939 :answer-field/choices 17592186149941] [:db/retract 17592186149939 :answer-field/choices 17592186149942] [:db/retract 17592186314656 :answer-field/choices 17592186313947] [:db/retract 17592186314340 :answer-field/choices 17592186312580] [:db/retract 17592186314139 :answer-field/choices 17592186313381] {:db/id 17592186152291 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7fd65812-f6ae-584d-bfe8-d11797aed930" "question-70cf3885-2e2c-5971-b49c-1988c3e0bb2b"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186151984 :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $y'' - 3y'+ 2y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y_1(x) = e^{x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n\nII. $y_2(x) = e^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation.\n\nIII. The general solution of the equation is $y=Ae^{x} + Be^{2x}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152292 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ab6bb605-4b84-5240-9d01-8856c6e45ebb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152293 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4d0ba009-0a0e-534d-98fc-35f0419611d1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7fd65812-f6ae-584d-bfe8-d11797aed930" :question/id #uuid "7fd65812-f6ae-584d-bfe8-d11797aed930" :question/math-academy-id "q-130000" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}-4y=0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}_{1}(x)=x{e}^{x}$ is a solution to the equation\n\nII. ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{2x}$ is a solution to the equation\n\nIII. The general solution of the equation is $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =(1+x){e}^{x} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =(2+x){e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n(2+x){e}^{x}-4(x{e}^{x})=(2-3x){e}^{x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement I is false.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =2{e}^{2x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n4{e}^{2x}-4{e}^{2x}=0.\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement II is true.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is not a solution while ${y}_{2}$ is a solution of the equation, hence $y=Ax{e}^{x}+B{e}^{2x}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement III is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9035e657-b711-5639-a608-83ef4fb511b6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9035e657-b711-5639-a608-83ef4fb511b6" :answer-field/id #uuid "9035e657-b711-5639-a608-83ef4fb511b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fda802d2-36b2-5ed7-834d-f564fbf27833" :answer-field/choices ["answer-78ece1af-ad7d-5ae8-b110-54b1d28cb817" "answer-96de1655-9970-5892-87e1-0ac2221ac207" "answer-0246f7ce-f1b2-5e93-8e63-e7393dc569b3" "answer-fda802d2-36b2-5ed7-834d-f564fbf27833" "answer-70e8c5bf-b371-5452-9286-8ac280de0cca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-78ece1af-ad7d-5ae8-b110-54b1d28cb817" :answer/id #uuid "78ece1af-ad7d-5ae8-b110-54b1d28cb817" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96de1655-9970-5892-87e1-0ac2221ac207" :answer/id #uuid "96de1655-9970-5892-87e1-0ac2221ac207" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0246f7ce-f1b2-5e93-8e63-e7393dc569b3" :answer/id #uuid "0246f7ce-f1b2-5e93-8e63-e7393dc569b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fda802d2-36b2-5ed7-834d-f564fbf27833" :answer/id #uuid "fda802d2-36b2-5ed7-834d-f564fbf27833" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70e8c5bf-b371-5452-9286-8ac280de0cca" :answer/id #uuid "70e8c5bf-b371-5452-9286-8ac280de0cca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-70cf3885-2e2c-5971-b49c-1988c3e0bb2b" :question/id #uuid "70cf3885-2e2c-5971-b49c-1988c3e0bb2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130004" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}-2y=0,$ where $x>0.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${y}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ is a solution to the equation\n\nII. ${y}_{2}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation\n\nIII. The general solution of the equation is $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's check each statement:\n\n- To determine whether ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to the differential equation, we substitute ${y}_{1}$ and its derivatives into the equation.\n\nFirst, we find the first and second derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{1}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}(\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}})+2x(-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})-2(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}=0.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution to the equation, and therefore statement I is true.\n\n- Similarly, we compute the derivatives of ${y}_{2}$ and substitute to the equation. Computing the derivatives yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's substitute ${y}_{2}(x)$ and its derivatives into the equation. We get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(12{x}^{2})+2x(4{x}^{3})-2{x}^{4}=18{x}^{4}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution to the equation, and therefore statement II is false.\n\n- So, ${y}_{1}$ is a solution but ${y}_{2}$ is not a solution of the equation, hence $y=\\frac{A}{{x}^{2}}+B{x}^{4}$ is not the general solution.\n\nTherefore, statement III is false." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b5729148-37a9-5323-892c-ea554a3ec7c8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b5729148-37a9-5323-892c-ea554a3ec7c8" :answer-field/id #uuid "b5729148-37a9-5323-892c-ea554a3ec7c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8c15b390-e3ab-578b-9938-8a4a3d2c7655" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2573a21a-8e89-50df-979f-28afe2a36547" "answer-8c15b390-e3ab-578b-9938-8a4a3d2c7655" "answer-c0d3143b-2b4d-55bb-b86b-df87737b53d0" "answer-9bc3278d-03ee-5ec6-8887-70c78218b07b" "answer-9d075126-4b78-5a5b-8783-75c3171a8fab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2573a21a-8e89-50df-979f-28afe2a36547" :answer/id #uuid "2573a21a-8e89-50df-979f-28afe2a36547" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c15b390-e3ab-578b-9938-8a4a3d2c7655" :answer/id #uuid "8c15b390-e3ab-578b-9938-8a4a3d2c7655" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0d3143b-2b4d-55bb-b86b-df87737b53d0" :answer/id #uuid "c0d3143b-2b4d-55bb-b86b-df87737b53d0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bc3278d-03ee-5ec6-8887-70c78218b07b" :answer/id #uuid "9bc3278d-03ee-5ec6-8887-70c78218b07b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d075126-4b78-5a5b-8783-75c3171a8fab" :answer/id #uuid "9d075126-4b78-5a5b-8783-75c3171a8fab" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ab6bb605-4b84-5240-9d01-8856c6e45ebb" :question/id #uuid "ab6bb605-4b84-5240-9d01-8856c6e45ebb" :question/math-academy-id "q-90696" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-3x}$ is a solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-9y=0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){e}^{-3x}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}-3u{e}^{-3x} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{e}^{-3x}-6{u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}+9u{e}^{-3x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{″}{e}^{-3x}-6{u}^{′}{e}^{-3x}+9u{e}^{-3x}-9u{e}^{-3x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{-3x}({u}^{″}-6{u}^{′}+9u-9u) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{-3x}({u}^{″}-6{u}^{′}) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${e}^{-3x}\\ne 0$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}-6{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}-6w=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw={c}_{1}{e}^{6x}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}={c}_{1}{e}^{6x}\\,⟹\\,u=\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{1}{e}^{6x}+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{e}^{-3x}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-3x}(\\frac{1}{6}{c}_{1}{e}^{6x}+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=6$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-3x}\\cdot {e}^{6x}={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=6\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4c6e7e2e-f610-5676-aec5-d60e36c7c4f2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4c6e7e2e-f610-5676-aec5-d60e36c7c4f2" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6e7e2e-f610-5676-aec5-d60e36c7c4f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3da93a06-f053-5c86-a2c8-81c4330a3717" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b0a79f06-5f3d-5f90-b216-f1e59a6b2bd8" "answer-6ffd0753-e57e-5d12-924f-8879651936b7" "answer-fdd3af73-a6f5-544b-af96-70b07bb9ad47" "answer-3da93a06-f053-5c86-a2c8-81c4330a3717" "answer-cc6c0735-9902-5936-acbf-abb753290129"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0a79f06-5f3d-5f90-b216-f1e59a6b2bd8" :answer/id #uuid "b0a79f06-5f3d-5f90-b216-f1e59a6b2bd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ffd0753-e57e-5d12-924f-8879651936b7" :answer/id #uuid "6ffd0753-e57e-5d12-924f-8879651936b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdd3af73-a6f5-544b-af96-70b07bb9ad47" :answer/id #uuid "fdd3af73-a6f5-544b-af96-70b07bb9ad47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3da93a06-f053-5c86-a2c8-81c4330a3717" :answer/id #uuid "3da93a06-f053-5c86-a2c8-81c4330a3717" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cc6c0735-9902-5936-acbf-abb753290129" :answer/id #uuid "cc6c0735-9902-5936-acbf-abb753290129" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-4d0ba009-0a0e-534d-98fc-35f0419611d1" :question/id #uuid "4d0ba009-0a0e-534d-98fc-35f0419611d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-79933" :question/problem "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={x}^{-2}$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+4y=0$ for $x>0,$ use reduction of order to find a second solution ${y}_{2}(x)$ to the equation, and write down the general solution." :question/worked-solution "According to the reduction of order method, we let ${y}_{2}=u(x){x}^{-2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating the above with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2}^{′} & ={u}^{′}{x}^{-2}-2u{x}^{-3} \\\\ {y}_{2}^{″} & ={u}^{″}{x}^{-2}-4{u}^{′}{x}^{-3}+6u{x}^{-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}({u}^{″}{x}^{-2}-4{u}^{′}{x}^{-3}+6u{x}^{-4})+5x({u}^{′}{x}^{-2}-2u{x}^{-3})+4u{x}^{-2} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}-4{u}^{′}{x}^{-1}+6u{x}^{-2}+5{u}^{′}{x}^{-1}-10u{x}^{-2}+4u{x}^{-2} & =0 \\\\ {u}^{″}+{u}^{′}{x}^{-1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x\\ne 0$ for $x>0,$ we must have\n\n$$\n{u}^{″}x+{u}^{′}=0.\n$$\n\nLet $w={u}^{′}.$ Then our equation becomes\n\n$$\n{w}^{′}x+w=0.\n$$\n\nThis is a separable equation that has the solution\n\n$$\nw=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{x}.\n$$\n\nBut since $w={u}^{′},$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=\\frac{{c}_{1}}{x}\\,⟹\\,u={c}_{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our expression for ${y}_{2}(x)=u{x}^{-2}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={x}^{-2}({c}_{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+{c}_{2}).\n$$\n\nSetting ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n{y}_{2}(x)={x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, because $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})={x}^{-5}\\ne 0,$ we know that ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are independent (you should verify this calculation yourself).\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=A{x}^{-2}+B{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-564f83a4-e64a-5a32-8a58-5a6072793073"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-564f83a4-e64a-5a32-8a58-5a6072793073" :answer-field/id #uuid "564f83a4-e64a-5a32-8a58-5a6072793073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-07ce657b-e482-5f99-bc7d-7195f7a26f4d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ebf1486-5cc5-5f08-9b5e-e0e154643134" "answer-a873b607-3f0b-5c6e-ba8c-a65ec6d7eec3" "answer-05fa078e-be12-5c3b-bea0-316dbe5fdadb" "answer-07ce657b-e482-5f99-bc7d-7195f7a26f4d" "answer-9bfec298-1d17-523e-a8e3-6399a0f68344"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ebf1486-5cc5-5f08-9b5e-e0e154643134" :answer/id #uuid "4ebf1486-5cc5-5f08-9b5e-e0e154643134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{-2}+Bx" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a873b607-3f0b-5c6e-ba8c-a65ec6d7eec3" :answer/id #uuid "a873b607-3f0b-5c6e-ba8c-a65ec6d7eec3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{-2}+Bx\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05fa078e-be12-5c3b-bea0-316dbe5fdadb" :answer/id #uuid "05fa078e-be12-5c3b-bea0-316dbe5fdadb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{-2}+B{x}^{-1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-07ce657b-e482-5f99-bc7d-7195f7a26f4d" :answer/id #uuid "07ce657b-e482-5f99-bc7d-7195f7a26f4d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{-2}+B{x}^{-2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bfec298-1d17-523e-a8e3-6399a0f68344" :answer/id #uuid "9bfec298-1d17-523e-a8e3-6399a0f68344" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{x}^{-2}+B{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152577 :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}-15y=-7{e}^{4x}\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{4x}$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{4x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({e}^{4x})^{′}=4{e}^{4x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(4{e}^{4x})^{′}=16{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(16{e}^{4x})-2(4{e}^{4x})-15({e}^{4x})=-7{e}^{4x}.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={e}^{4x}$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x{e}^{4x})^{′}={e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =({e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x})^{′}=8{e}^{4x}+16x{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n(8{e}^{4x}+16x{e}^{4x})-2({e}^{4x}+4x{e}^{4x})-15(x{e}^{4x})=-7{e}^{4x}.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x{e}^{4x}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x}+{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149944 :answer-field/correct 17592186149945 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149947 :answer-field/correct 17592186149948 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149955 :answer-field/correct "answer-243e57c9-66d3-57a3-8eda-0a620df3bf86" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7a6a2534-2107-5651-a152-891cafe89c13" "answer-c41c8261-80c9-5a5b-8f42-0d5bf3de5a07" "answer-243e57c9-66d3-57a3-8eda-0a620df3bf86" "answer-10f3beec-4202-5dab-a3d5-826a80ea36b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7a6a2534-2107-5651-a152-891cafe89c13" :answer/id #uuid "7a6a2534-2107-5651-a152-891cafe89c13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c41c8261-80c9-5a5b-8f42-0d5bf3de5a07" :answer/id #uuid "c41c8261-80c9-5a5b-8f42-0d5bf3de5a07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{-5x}+B{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-243e57c9-66d3-57a3-8eda-0a620df3bf86" :answer/id #uuid "243e57c9-66d3-57a3-8eda-0a620df3bf86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10f3beec-4202-5dab-a3d5-826a80ea36b3" :answer/id #uuid "10f3beec-4202-5dab-a3d5-826a80ea36b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{3x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186149950 :answer-field/correct "answer-201d8ac2-9e51-5cf5-98c1-c1ef06a0df77" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9a855e4c-2e4a-569e-b11a-653e7305e4f2" "answer-7b60cf07-89bc-5ff0-af50-91a09012fa23" "answer-422031fe-5ff8-51b0-a1c9-b5e22dbccec0" "answer-201d8ac2-9e51-5cf5-98c1-c1ef06a0df77"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a855e4c-2e4a-569e-b11a-653e7305e4f2" :answer